Set Strict Testing Rules
Tests must fail when the code has a bug — no simulated or rewritten-to-pass tests
Specify the test framework, fixture conventions, and where tests live
Enforce a "Never" List
No hardcoded secrets
No mutable default arguments
No bare except: blocks
No generic data structures (raw dicts/lists) where typed models fit
No optional types unless genuinely needed
Define project-specific forbidden patterns
Require Strict Typing
All function parameters, return types, and non-obvious variables must be annotated
Use modern syntax (int | None, not Optional[int]; list, not List)
Agents overuse optionals and generic structures if you don't constrain them
Write Actionable Rules, Not Aspirations
✅ "Use pathlib for all file operations"
❌ "Write clean, maintainable code"
Short do/don't examples for non-obvious rules only
Maintain and Evolve the File
Make the agent document edge cases and lessons learned as it encounters them
Monitor file bloat — prune aggressively after each growth cycle
Treat the file as code: review changes in PRs, version in git
Keep a build plan with milestones; refresh it as context compacts over long sessions



